    fieldname: new UntypedFormControl("", Validators.required),
});
I want to focus the first element on start."

model_response:
 To focus the first element in an Angular FormGroup on start, you can use the `focus()` method on the first element of the FormGroup. Here's an example:
```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { FormGroup, FormControl, Validators } from '@angular/forms';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  template: `
    <form [formGroup]="form">
      <div formGroupName="fieldname">
        <input formControlName="fieldname" type="text" />
      </div>
    </form>
  `,
})
export class AppComponent {
  form: FormGroup;

  constructor() {
    this.form = new FormGroup({
      fieldname: new FormControl('', Validators.required),
    });

    // Focus the first element on start
    const firstElement = document.querySelector('input[formControlName="fieldname"]');
    if (firstElement) {
      firstElement.focus();
    }
  }
}
```
In this example, the `formGroupName` attribute is used to group the `fieldname` input element under the `fieldname` FormControl. The `focus()` method is then called on the first element of the FormGroup, which is the `fieldname` input element. This will focus the input element on start.

